{
  "ruleChain": {
    "additionalInfo": {
      "description": "fishpump rule chain, modelled on the Root Rule Chain: Message Type Switch then Save Timeseries, Save Client Attributes, RPC and Log. Telemetry first passes the check Has alarm_event. Plain telemetry is saved. Alarm events (alarm_event at top level, or inside values with a ts) go through: fetch the server attribute last_alarm_event (boot_id and seq), normalize and dedupe (drop when boot_id is equal and seq is not greater than the stored one), route, then Create Alarm (type rule_ plus the rule id; critical is CRITICAL, warning is WARNING, info is INDETERMINATE; details are the event) or Clear Alarm (same type), then save last_alarm_event as a SERVER_SCOPE attribute. The source of truth is this file and tb_setup.py imports it by name."
    },
    "name": "fishpump",
    "type": "CORE",
    "firstRuleNodeId": null,
    "root": false,
    "debugMode": false,
    "configuration": null
  },
  "metadata": {
